                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c943087b-ee7d-4ea4-830f-5826d8f65c62",
                        "source_entry_id": "b04b3aee-571e-336e-8303-f26a2b9ecc46",
                        "source_sense_id": "f1ce425d-78f4-3e5a-b8d7-6c2d6da44945",
                        "target_lang_word": "jeremiad",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "jeremiad",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e0b97974-8079-3952-877c-f1f5c6b9dae0",
                                        "entry_id": "ee583dbd-3f94-3399-9b90-abf5bee9f4cb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A long speech or prose work that bitterly laments the state of society and its morals, and often contains a prophecy of its coming downfall."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2a3210c4-86fe-4330-89d4-22fd44ccf87d",
                                                "sense_id": "e0b97974-8079-3952-877c-f1f5c6b9dae0",
                                                "text": "\"Father Maguire,\" he said in the broadest of Cork brogues, without the ghost of a smile on his grave Irish face, \"is it a song yez wantin'? Well, thin, it's just a jeremiad I 'd be singin' yez, an' not another song at all, at all.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5ac1dbb7-154c-4c32-b422-e077107318a5",
                                                "sense_id": "e0b97974-8079-3952-877c-f1f5c6b9dae0",
                                                "text": "“This is precisely the manner of Balkanization that Schlesinger cautioned us about in his prescient jeremiad on multiculturalism, The Disuniting of America.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f3371ede-a396-406d-8660-76fe134e2bca",
                                                "sense_id": "e0b97974-8079-3952-877c-f1f5c6b9dae0",
                                                "text": "Cannes is smacking its lips in anticipation of filmmaker and provocateur Michael Moore's latest jeremiad against the US administration, which receives its premiere at the film festival today."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3d196f9b-d1f8-4e43-991d-7d400cea4281",
                                                "sense_id": "e0b97974-8079-3952-877c-f1f5c6b9dae0",
                                                "text": "His warnings ignored in Washington, Dalio issued more jeremiads to his clients. “If the economy goes down, it will not be a typical recession,” his newsletter said in January, 2008."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c5d463bc-0f40-4020-95de-8b684c79eac4",
                                                "sense_id": "e0b97974-8079-3952-877c-f1f5c6b9dae0",
                                                "text": "What few of us realised at the time was that Osborne, while endorsing most of Jimmy’s jeremiads, also had a sneaking sympathy for his father-in-law, Colonel Redfern, an upper-class relic of the Raj."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "36ba3d9f-8764-4f2b-9aca-bd7206d607ca",
                        "source_entry_id": "b04b3aee-571e-336e-8303-f26a2b9ecc46",
                        "source_sense_id": "f1ce425d-78f4-3e5a-b8d7-6c2d6da44945",
                        "target_lang_word": "jérémiade",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "jérémiade",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "aafc5876-3ac6-320f-acce-ec8285694ea5",
                                        "entry_id": "00abcfc5-ba63-3c4c-839c-37e1ed4752bd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Plainte fréquente et importune."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "familiar"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1ce2cd15-0c4b-43f5-b14e-07f6b90b3079",
                                                "sense_id": "aafc5876-3ac6-320f-acce-ec8285694ea5",
                                                "text": "Partant de ce point, ne sommes-nous pas autorisé à nous demander ce que signifient ces jérémiades forcées qui consistent à déplorer continuellement le sort de nos anciennes races ?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e2fd29a0-aee0-4057-a0b0-d6888155f889",
                                                "sense_id": "aafc5876-3ac6-320f-acce-ec8285694ea5",
                                                "text": "Seulement celles-ci sont subordonnées à une histoire d'amour; le mythe permet d'éviter la jérémiade syndicaliste."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "63c6d202-0a0e-4bfa-8022-1f78a8275261",
                                                "sense_id": "aafc5876-3ac6-320f-acce-ec8285694ea5",
                                                "text": "Entre jérémiades et désinformation, le président sortant a-t-il servi la cause des deux candidats républicains qui espèrent s’emparer des derniers sièges du Sénat?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
